Dunamos the Sorcerer      St:18 Dx:18 Co:16 In:23 Wi:23 Ch:18  Chaotic
Astral Plane $:0  HP:228(228) Pw:265(348) AC:-18 Xp:21/10095742 T:63199
[was AC:-27 until I zapped +oDeath and took out Anhur's astral priest]

This is the first time I ascended wishless/polyless. I'm a natural
for this conduct because I'm a pack rat and enjoy the process of
sorting through all the objects and squeezing out all the usefulness.
A lot of things went right for me this game (notably getting SD
scales and a MM) to help wishless succeed. My HP Pw AC and XL were
certainly all much lower than in previous games, and I had more
"holes" in my equipment list when starting the ascension run than
I'd like. Had a t-shirt but nothing to enchant it with!

The other big difference from previous games is that I never found
+oCharm; normally pets are a big part of my strategy, not to mention
the spell's usefulness when surrounded. I needed my MM's charges for
other stuff, so I made do with cats dogs and horses, and ended up
with one that polymorphed and grew to a very powerful storm giant.

Everyone who says that =oConflict makes the planes easier is absolutely
right. Can't believe I didn't try this before.

The Plane of Air is the hardest part of the game for me, but at least
I generally know what to do. The Plane of Water is the most annoying;
I still do not "get" how the portal moves. The Bell of Opening doesn't
seem to do anything, even when the "oYendor is giving clues. In all 3
ascensions I've had to wait to stumble across the portal; good for HP
and Pw, but hard to stay careful/patient when you're so near the end.

